# honestweek sidecars (intermediate working artifacts — never published)
honestweek.draft.json
honestweek.prompts.json
honestweek.prompts.json.tmp-*
honestweek.prompts.json.lock
honestweek.prompt-items.json
honestweek.prompt-items.json.tmp-*
honestweek.curated.json
honestweek.curated.json.tmp-*
honestweek.digest.pending.json
honestweek.digest.pending.json.tmp-*
honestweek.carry.json
honestweek.carry.json.tmp-*
honestweek.carry.pending.json
honestweek.carry.pending.json.tmp-*
honestweek.items.json
honestweek.history.json
honestweek.history.json.tmp-*
# `harvest` keeps raw candidate nouns here, and Run with Codex keeps what codex wrote about
# each session here. Both add themselves to the .gitignore of the folder they're written in;
# these lines cover running them in this repo too.
honestweek.harvest.json
honestweek.codex-judgments/

# `mine` writes unpublished post drafts here by default. They are working artifacts
# with unverified claims in them; a destination that wants them tracked sets
# mine.draft.dir to a path inside its own repo instead.
honestweek.drafts/

# NOTE: honestweek.findings.json — the `mine` decision ledger — is intentionally NOT
# ignored. It is the only record of which findings you already declined, and losing it
# means every past decision gets offered back to you as new. Everything in it is
# de-identified and redacted before it is written. Its atomic-write temp files ARE
# ignored, like every sidecar's above.
honestweek.findings.json.tmp-*

# The user's own config MAY contain private repo paths and redaction terms,
# so it is ignored by default. To track it in git (e.g. a personal dotfiles
# repo where that is acceptable), delete the line below or add a negation:
#   !honestweek.config.json
honestweek.config.json

# NOTE: honestweek.config.example.json is the tracked, shareable template —
# it is intentionally NOT ignored.

# Dependencies (there should be none at runtime, but never commit these)
node_modules/

# The tarball `npm pack` writes when checking what a release would ship
*.tgz

# The demo week (tools/demo-week.mjs) when written into the repo: logs and a nested repo
.demo-out/

# Local working files for this repo: hand-offs, research, test logs, worktrees and
# prototypes built from real sessions. They stay on the machine that made them.
/.claude/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.vscode/
